---
title: "A theme-aware figure"
---

A figure can ship a `dark=` variant that swaps with the page theme, so a screenshot or a
diagram whose colours are baked in stays legible in both light and dark. Toggle the theme
and the image below swaps; there is still just one figure, one caption, one gallery entry.

![A model fit, light and dark.](fit-b.png){#fig-themed dark="fit-c.png"}

A plain figure with no `dark=` is unchanged:

![The same fit, single variant.](fit-a.png){#fig-plain}
